WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.068
Welcome to Hamerschlag Hall.

2
00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:06.473
This is the home to the College
of Engineering, also known as CIT.

3
00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.943
This is the largest
CMU undergraduate college by enrollment

4
00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.579
and academically there are six main majors

5
00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.248
with the option for four additional engineering majors,

6
00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.684
as well as an integrated master's degree program,

7
00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.887
which could be a 3+1 or a 4+1.

8
00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.190
Right now we are in front of Tech Spark,
which is a makerspace

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.227
that is part of the 60+
makerspaces is on campus.

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.596
Any student can get certified
to make stuff here

11
00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.297
as long as you pass a course on that.

12
00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.633
You are responsible
for bringing your own materials

13
00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.603
and you can make pretty much anything
except for weapons.

14
00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.004
Now, at this point in our tour,

15
00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:41.307
we have done quite a bit of walking,
so it's probably time to talk about food.

16
00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.843
We have a special food system
here called the BLOCK System,

17
00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.346
where each block
is a meal with a side and a drink.

18
00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.314
For those with allergy needs,

19
00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:52.852
we also have something called Nourish,
which is an allergen friendly kitchen.

20
00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:57.290
We also don't have central dining halls,
but rather 30+ eateries across campus.

21
00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.926
And all first years are required
to be on a meal plan.

22
00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:04.397
And the motivation for this format is
kind of twofold, the first being social.

23
00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:08.401
So having a bunch of different eateries
scattered across campus makes it really

24
00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.272
easy to send out invitations like,
hey, let's meet at this place for food.

25
00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.742
That really leads way
for really organic human interactions.

26
00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.844
And the second reason is that
it allows yourself

27
00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.814
to explore without having
basic human needs getting in the way.

28
00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.116
And then in your second year,
when you've pruned your hobbies,

29
00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.518
you can develop your culinary
career as you see fit.

